version 3. See COPYING for the full text.

Version 3 rather than upstream's version 2, and not a choice:

  - cpuminer-opt, which most of this miner is, is offered under "version 2
    of the License, or (at your option) any later version". The later
    option is taken here.

  - The CUDA and HIP kernels under cuda/ derive from suprminer, which is
    GPL version 3 and carries Apache-2.0 material as well. Apache-2.0 can
    be conveyed under GPLv3 and cannot be conveyed under GPLv2, so a
    combined work including it has no version 2 form to distribute.

Upstream's GPLv2 text is kept as COPYING.GPLv2, since the files that carry
a "version 2 or later" notice still carry it and that notice is what makes
the upgrade above legitimate.
